  "id": "wf4-guard-conflicted-action-approval-route",
  "description": "On the APPROVAL route pointing at a duplicated action, the guard halts before the Approval Gate runs.",
  "why_it_exists": "On the real MAT-20260101-002 snapshot the Actions register held TWO generations of rows written 39 minutes apart, so six action_ids each resolved to two rows carrying different action_types, recipients and channels. Approval Gate re-queried by action_id and simply took the last match, meaning WF4 could draft, approve and send against a row nobody chose - for example sending a CONTACT_INSURER letter to a car park manager. The Integrity Guard refuses to choose between duplicate rows, and Verify Selected Row re-checks the chosen row immediately before any writer or Gmail node runs. The approval route narrows scope to the single action the approval names, so this proves the narrowed scope still catches the duplication rather than passing it through.",
